  20: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
  21:     """
  22:     Move each colored object vertically until it touches the matching top or bottom border bar.
  23: 
  24:     Input structure:
  25:     - The background is the dominant color.
  26:     - The top row is a full-width bar in one foreground color and the bottom row is a full-width bar in another.
  27:     - All other foreground pixels are 8-connected monochrome objects whose color matches one of those bars.
  28: 
  29:     Rule:
  30:     - Top-bar-colored objects move upward so their bbox top is row 1.
  31:     - Bottom-bar-colored objects move downward so their bbox bottom is the row above the bottom bar.
  32:     - A downward-moving one-column segment whose landing overlaps its source becomes the continuous vertical segment swept between them.
  33: 
  34:     Key insight:
  35:     The horizontal bars are destination anchors: color determines which border an object slides toward, while columns and object shape are otherwise preserved.
  36:     """
